WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
A dish passes through four cooks, a minute each.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.600
A kitchen fits only two cooks.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.083
Across the yard to the other kitchen: 3 more minutes.

4
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:17.217
This split: 7.

5
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.810
Another split, and everyone still fits.

6
00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.721
But it crosses the yard twice: 10 minutes.

7
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:29.721
Speed depends on how often the longest route crosses the yard.

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.467
A banquet: twelve steps, three starts, two finished dishes.

9
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:47.489
Each kitchen holds four; crossing the yard is still 3 minutes.

10
00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:50.511
The longest route: five steps.

11
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.536
Each step gets a number: its earliest minute.

12
00:00:55.536 --> 00:00:58.602
The starts are 1; then it adds up.

13
00:00:58.602 --> 00:01:02.136
g shares a kitchen with all before it: 3.

14
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.283
Seven steps before i, room for three.

15
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:10.750
b is across the yard: 4 + 3 = 7.

16
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.350
i's earliest: minute 7.

17
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.600
j is 7 too.

18
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.000
Both finished dishes: 8.

19
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.689
These are only times; no kitchens yet.

20
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.356
k's kitchen needs g and j; so does l's.

21
00:01:33.356 --> 00:01:35.956
So each makes its own.

22
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.833
Work back from the dishes: whatever is missing gets its own kitchen.

23
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:52.411
Eight kitchens, twenty cooks, twelve steps.

24
00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:56.100
Both dishes come out at minute 8.

25
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:04.737
No copies? Try every split: the best is 10.

26
00:02:04.737 --> 00:02:08.203
Eight more hands, two minutes faster.

27
00:02:08.203 --> 00:02:11.226
The speed is paid for in space.

28
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.560
On a chip: a signal that leaves its region waits longer.

29
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Speed is set by the longest route.

30
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.500
Each boundary crossed adds D.

31
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:40.500
Copies buy speed, and cost area.

32
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:48.500
The last module: compare all eight on the home page.

33
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
In the lab below, step through the labels and the recovered instances.
